<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;" id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
    <div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;">
      <details class="sc-faq" open>
      <summary>What makes MEMS and sensor assembly different?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">The sensing element must continue interacting with its environment after assembly. This requires low-stress die attach and package structures that protect the device while maintaining pressure, optical, gas or other required access.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What sensor types can Hana assemble?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">MEMS-based pressure, inertial, acoustic and gas sensors, optical proximity, ambient-light, color and time-of-flight sensors, humidity and temperature sensors, and LiDAR sensor packages, in cavity, open-cavity, LCC and custom package formats.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Which sensor packages has Hana built?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Examples include open-cavity W185QFN LiDAR packages with a glass lid at 10 × 5.2 mm and 27 × 16 mm, a pre-molded W32 DFN oil pressure sensor package made with film-assisted molding, a 5 × 5 mm cavity QFN pressure sensor package with a port hole in the lid, and open-cavity SOIC and 2.5 × 2.5 mm DFN humidity and temperature sensor packages. Sizes are listed in the <a href="#sensor-packages" style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:600;">sensor package table</a> on this page.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What packaging types do you offer?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Hana supports cavity and open-cavity packages, media-access / ported packages, and selective gel or glob-top protection. Optical sensors use clear transfer mold, metal or plastic caps and film-assist molding, covered on the <a href="/capabilities/osat/optical-packaging" style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:600;">Clear &amp; Optical Packaging</a> page.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>How do you protect sensor accuracy?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Low-stress die attach and stress-decoupling adhesives help limit mechanical loading on the sensing element. Attach materials and cure profiles are selected per device, and the process is developed and qualified during first-article builds.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Can Hana test and calibrate sensors during production?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Electrical and functional test can be integrated into the manufacturing process, including gas and MEMS functional test for medical sensor assemblies. Test and calibration requirements are defined per program.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What quality systems apply?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">ISO 9001 applies group-wide, with ISO 13485 for medical sensors and IATF 16949 for automotive sensors, in ESD-controlled areas meeting ANSI/ESD S20.20.</div>
    </details>
    </div>
